    "show_share": true,
    "description": "More patients control blood pressure well through medication if doctor to patient communication is improved. Researchers at Aga Khan University (AKU) have found evidence suggesting increased consultation time with physicians and improved communication are factors that may step up patient cooperation in adhering to blood pressure control medication. This week's British Medical Journal has published findings of a study included in AKU's Hypertension Project, which is being conducted in 12 communities in Karachi.",
